{
  "id": "method-of-constant-stimuli",
  "term": "method of constant stimuli",
  "definition": "The method of constant stimuli is a psychophysical procedure for finding a person’s point of subjective equality by presenting a standard stimulus alongside a set of comparison stimuli spread at fixed intervals across a range. The comparison stimuli are shown one at a time in random order, usually many times, and the person judges which stimulus has more or less of the target quality.",
